{
 "tickets": [
  {
   "body": "Hi, one of our patients wants to use a brand new local pharmacy that just opened up down the street, but it's not showing up when we try to look it up in the system directory. Can you tell us how we can manually add this custom pharmacy entry so we can send their prescriptions there?",
   "id": "gen-091",
   "subject": "Pharmacy directory search and custom additions"
  },
  {
   "body": "The online payment screen on the portal is completely broken right now and none of our patients can pay their balances. Please fix this outage immediately so we can process transactions again.",
   "id": "gen-092",
   "subject": "Portal credit card processing is down"
  },
  {
   "body": "Good morning. We've been trying to help a few different patients use the online payment portal this week to clear their copays and balances ahead of their scheduled appointments, but they keep running into credit card processing declines on the checkout screen. We tried testing it ourselves from the front desk using a test card, and it keeps spinning for a few seconds before throwing a generic error code without specifying what went wrong. Could you please clarify what might be causing these declines and how we can guide our patients through successful payments?",
   "id": "gen-093",
   "subject": "Troubleshooting online portal payment declines"
  },
  {
   "body": "To whom it may concern, our billing department is currently unable to batch and submit insurance claims due to a system-wide failure affecting the clearinghouse submission module. Kindly investigate this service disruption as a matter of urgency.",
   "id": "gen-094",
   "subject": "Urgent: Electronic insurance claim submission failure"
  },
  {
   "body": "I am so terribly sorry to have to reach out about this, but we had a bad mix-up with a prescription renewal request this morning for a patient, initials J.S. The pharmacy sent over a renewal for a medication the patient no longer takes, and when I tried to process the electronic refill request, I must have clicked the wrong button because it transmitted an incorrect dosage to their pharmacy before I caught it. We managed to call the pharmacist right away to halt it, but I'm quite shaken about how easily the renewal got linked to the wrong active medication line in the chart. Could someone please help me understand how to properly link and manage these incoming pharmacy requests so this doesn't happen again?",
   "id": "gen-095",
   "subject": "Apologies - prescription renewal transmission error"
  },
  {
   "body": "Need instructions on how to correct a misapplied insurance payment that spans multiple invoice lines.",
   "id": "gen-096",
   "subject": "Correcting misapplied payments across invoice lines"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hello, I am writing because something very strange happened with our digital intake forms this morning and I am quite worried about patient privacy. A patient came in and mentioned that when they were filling out their medical history questionnaire online last night, part of the previous person's emergency contact details seemed to flash on their screen before their own form loaded. We use custom intake forms that we published to our portal link, and I don't know if this means records are getting crossed or if data was visible to someone who shouldn't see it. Could you please look into how our form field validation and session caching are working right now? We want to make sure no confidential information was exposed.",
   "id": "gen-097",
   "subject": "Concern regarding intake form data visibility"
  },
  {
   "body": "Why is it so difficult to route lab results to covering physicians in this software? Every time Dr. Smith is out of office, I waste twenty minutes trying to figure out how to assign incoming lab work to another doctor before I can sign off on it. Can you please provide clear instructions on how to handle this workflow without getting blocked by error prompts?",
   "id": "gen-098",
   "subject": "Trouble routing lab results to covering physicians"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hello, we are receiving several out-of-stock notices from local pharmacies for a few common medications. Could you please remind me of the steps required to process these substitution alerts and switch the prescriptions over to alternative therapeutic agents within the software?",
   "id": "gen-099",
   "subject": "Handling medication substitutions and out-of-stock alerts"
  },
  {
   "body": "Please update the provider scheduling module to reflect the correct working hours and calendar blocks for our clinical staff starting next month.",
   "id": "gen-100",
   "subject": "Request to update provider working hours"
  }
 ]
}
